@@ -6,3 +6,11 @@ package holds the order book, in TypeScript; the shop's website and its staff to
 `src/index.ts`.
 
 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Discount codes
+
+`orders.applyCode(orderNumber, code)` puts a code on an order; a second code replaces the first. `SPRING10` takes 10 %
+off the items (a half cent rounds up); `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € off, only on items of 30.00 € or more. An unknown code,
+or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused and the order is left as it was. The discount never touches shipping,
+which is still decided on the items before any discount. `totals` shows it as `discountCents` (0 without a code);
+`totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping.
